{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Understand this, you who forget El</b> — they are the thieves and the adulterers and the slanderers, and He likened the evil that shall come upon them to the tearing of the lion from whose hand none delivers, for the shepherd can deliver from the bear or from the wolf, but torn prey from whose hand none delivers — for the shepherd can deliver from the bear, but not as one is delivered from the mouth of the lion."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {0 "The Hebrew text appears to contain a corruption or dittography: the phrase 'שאין מציל מידו כי הרועה יכול להציל' recurs with slight variation, suggesting a scribal duplication; translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:32.137035117Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}